      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Vascular disease is the most common cause of male erectile dysfunction (ED). Phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5) inhibitors are effective in up to 80% of men but are contraindicated in the presence of oral nitrates, because of a potentially severe hypotensive interaction."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIMS",
          "content": "To see if stable coronary disease patients with ED could have their oral nitrates discontinued to allow safe use of a PDE5 inhibitor."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Prospective study of 425 men with ED and cardiac disease conducted in an outpatient cardiac sexual advice clinic."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES",
          "content": "Discontinuation of oral nitrates to facilitate subsequent use of PDE5 therapy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Oral nitrates were being used by 88 (21%) coronary artery disease patients all of whom were clinically stable. Fifty-five (63%) of these men with a good exercise ability had their nitrates discontinued in the presence of continuing beta-blockade or calcium antagonist therapy. They were reviewed 1 week later. Only three restarted their nitrate therapy because of an increase in symptoms. Forty-nine of the 52 men no longer taking nitrates were treated with a PDE5 inhibitor which was effective in 22 out of 26 (85%) patients who have completed follow-up. Fifteen patients are currently undergoing clinic follow-up in order to optimize treatment, and nine patients have continued therapy with their family doctors. Importantly, there have been no adverse cardiac events."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Oral nitrates can be discontinued in the presence of continuing beta-blockade and/or calcium antagonist therapy in stable coronary disease patients with ED to allow for the safe use of PDE5 inhibitors."
        }
      ]},
